WEBVTT

NOTE Draft timing. Synchronise to the final recorded narration before release.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.111
It's only twelve euro.

00:00:03.111 --> 00:00:07.000
So why doesn't it match?

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.727
Sometimes the smallest discrepancy raises the biggest question.

00:00:11.727 --> 00:00:20.000
Can we explain every number, from the original invoice to the final bank transaction?

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.083
That's what drew me to DataPoint Ireland.

00:00:24.083 --> 00:00:34.000
Your work brings together accounting, payroll, reporting and business analytics to help businesses make more informed decisions.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.667
Then I read your Accounts and Payroll Analyst vacancy.

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:48.000
Instead of simply listing my skills in another CV, I wanted to demonstrate how I approach the work.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:01:00.000
So I built LedgerPoint, an independent finance operations prototype inspired by DataPoint's work and the responsibilities of this position.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.207
It brings invoices, reconciliation and financial reporting into one demonstration.

00:01:06.207 --> 00:01:11.793
Here, a twelve-euro bank debit has no ledger match.

00:01:11.793 --> 00:01:18.000
LedgerPoint flags it for investigation rather than inventing an explanation.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.182
I'm Shaik Arham Saquib.

00:01:20.182 --> 00:01:28.364
With experience in business intelligence and data analytics, this is how I chose to apply.

00:01:28.364 --> 00:01:30.000
Welcome to LedgerPoint.

